text.section:
The Supreme Court shall by rule, which may from time to time be amended, supplemented or repealed, but which shall be uniform in its application throughout the Commonwealth, designate the nontraffic offenses for which a pretrial waiver of appearance, plea of guilty and fine payment may be accepted. Such offenses shall not include:

Indictable offenses;


Class 1 or Class 2 misdemeanors;


Offenses which involve moral turpitude;


Any offenses involving injury to persons;


Any offense punishable by incarceration or by a fine of more than $500.
